statement:
Let P, n ∈ ℕ and t ∈ ℝ, and write Hⁿ = μHE[n]. Assume ψ : ℝ^{n+1} → ℝ^P is C¹, V ⊆ ℝ^{n+1} is open, ψ is injective on V, Dψ(y) is injective for y ∈ V, and F : ℝ^{n+1} → ℝ is C¹. Then there are open sets U_j ⊆ ℝⁿ, points a_j ∈ ℝⁿ, radii r_j ∈ ℝ and maps χ_j : ℝⁿ → ℝ^P (j ∈ ℕ) such that for every j:
- closedBall(a_j, r_j) ⊆ U_j;
- χ_j is C¹ on U_j and injective on U_j;
- χ_j(U_j) is countably n-rectifiable, and Hⁿ(χ_j(closedBall(a_j, r_j))) < ∞;
- for every w ∈ U_j, Dχ_j(w) is injective, and there is y ∈ V with ψ(y) = χ_j(w), F(y) = t and DF(y) ≠ 0 such that Dχ_j(w)(ℝⁿ) = Dψ(y)(ℝ^{n+1}) ∩ (ℝv)^⊥ for every v ∈ Dψ(y)(ℝ^{n+1}) with ⟨v, Dψ(y)e⟩ = DF(y)e for all e.
Moreover ψ({y ∈ V : F(y) = t, DF(y) ≠ 0}) ⊆ ⋃_j χ_j(ball(a_j, r_j)).
